        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23638587?u=6d1f4ed9b2481fd4af374eb927f9a73602c53ba5&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/jyn514/rfcs/blob/crate-attr/text/3791-crate-attr.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">cc <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2905664297\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/138287\" data-hovercard-type=\"issue\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rust/issues/138287/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/issues/138287\">rust-lang/rust#138287</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Differences from the current nightly implementation (note that this section is non-normative):</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li><code class=\"notranslate\">-A -W -D -F</code> become aliases for <code class=\"notranslate\">crate-attr</code></li>\n<li>Attributes are prepended, not appended.</li>\n<li>Everything about how this interacts with doctests (see <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"2923808363\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/3791\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3791/hovercard?comment_id=1999037718&amp;comment_type=review_comment\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3791#discussion_r1999037718\">#3791 (comment)</a>)</li>\n<li>The attribute shares the same Span as the crate root. In particular <code class=\"notranslate\">file!</code> behaves properly now and the edition is no longer always 2015.</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3791",
            "title": "RFC: `--crate-attr`",
            "date_modified": "2025-03-30T15:09:00.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-17T05:38:21.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "jyn514",
                "url": "https://github.com/jyn514"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1464942?u=0d7b571220d08172a442dbcafbe5d3dd3b45c786&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The example in the API conventions (in imperative) contradicts the text (use third person). This PR corrects the example to fit the text description.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/vigna/rfcs/blob/fix_third_person/text/0505-api-comment-conventions.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3787",
            "title": "Make examples coherent with text",
            "date_modified": "2025-03-10T08:39:46.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-07T10:44:26.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "vigna",
                "url": "https://github.com/vigna"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9914262?u=6d397d57ea18944924ce4d9c107b7dad87ff0c0e&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">The <code class=\"notranslate\">std::num::NonZero&lt;T&gt;</code> type allows non-zero integer semantics to be clearly expressed. Yet this<br>\ntype is only seamlessly usable if all APIs with non-zero semantics use this type, due to required<br>\nto/from conversion at any API boundary that differs in its use of <code class=\"notranslate\">NonZero</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The burden of these conversions is especially heavy in tests and examples. This RFC proposes new<br>\ncoercions to facilitate implicit conversion to <code class=\"notranslate\">NonZero</code> from integral constants, simplifying usage<br>\nin tests and examples, where succinctness and readability are paramount.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/sandersaares/rust-lang-rfcs/blob/u/sasaares/const-nonzero-ergonomics/text/3786-const-nonzero-ergonomics.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3786",
            "title": "RFC: const ergonomics for NonZero<T>",
            "date_modified": "2025-03-24T07:08:59.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-07T09:22:17.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "sandersaares",
                "url": "https://github.com/sandersaares"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63151578?u=0a831ef01c1b17a592d62367cce371f36262f66b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC proposes a mechanism for crates to define default bounds on generics. By specifying these defaults at the crate level we can reduce the need for verbose and repetitive <code class=\"notranslate\">?Trait</code> annotations while maintaining backward compatibility and enabling future language evolution.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">It is targeted at supporting migrations from default being <code class=\"notranslate\">Trait</code> to <code class=\"notranslate\">?Trait</code>, where <code class=\"notranslate\">Trait</code> represents some assumption that is present everywhere but is not really exercised a lot, such as <code class=\"notranslate\">Forget</code>, <code class=\"notranslate\">size = stride</code> etc. Features like <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/2984\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/2984/hovercard\"><code class=\"notranslate\">DynSized</code></a>, as well as <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/1861\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/1861/hovercard\"><code class=\"notranslate\">extern types</code></a>, are out of the scope of this RFC, because it does not fit into this category. <code class=\"notranslate\">DynSized</code> is not retracting mostly unexercised assumptions in order to make it <code class=\"notranslate\">?DynSized</code> the default.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Primary use case is <a href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3782\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3782/hovercard\"><code class=\"notranslate\">Forget</code> marker trait</a>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Ddystopia/rfcs/blob/local-default-bounds/text/0000-local-default-generic-bounds.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-local-default-bounds/22453\" rel=\"nofollow\">Pre-RFC thread</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3783",
            "title": "Local Default Bounds to assist `Forget` and other `?Trait`.",
            "date_modified": "2025-03-25T14:46:44.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-01T13:19:44.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Ddystopia",
                "url": "https://github.com/Ddystopia"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/63151578?u=0a831ef01c1b17a592d62367cce371f36262f66b&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Add a <code class=\"notranslate\">Forget</code> marker trait indicating whether it is safe to skip the destructor before the value of a type exits the scope and basic utilities to work with <code class=\"notranslate\">!Forget</code> types. Introduce a seamless migration route for the standard library and ecosystem.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Ddystopia/rfcs/blob/forget-marker-trait/text/0000-forget-marker-trait.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://internals.rust-lang.org/t/pre-rfc-forget-marker-trait/22456\" rel=\"nofollow\">Pre-RFC thread</a></p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Unresolved questions</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\"> Unsafe guarantee that <code class=\"notranslate\">!Forget</code> gives to the <code class=\"notranslate\">unsafe</code> code is already fulfilled for all <code class=\"notranslate\">'static</code> types. Because of that, it doesn't really make a lot of sense to have <code class=\"notranslate\">!Forget + 'static</code>, it is still sound to <code class=\"notranslate\">mem::forget</code> that type. Should we force <code class=\"notranslate\">impl&lt;T: 'static&gt; Forget for T</code> then?</li>\n</ul>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3782",
            "title": "`Forget` marker trait",
            "date_modified": "2025-03-30T23:22:24.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-03-01T13:16:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "Ddystopia",
                "url": "https://github.com/Ddystopia"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18085551?u=d28b23fc7492d25f5224c6133ee73e278a75fdc6&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/kxxt/rfcs/blob/crate-changelog-field/text/0000-crate-changelog-field.md\">Rendered</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This is the second attempt to introduce the <code class=\"notranslate\">changelog</code> field into crate manifest.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Previous attempt: <a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"253131429\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/issues/2129\" data-hovercard-type=\"pull_request\" data-hovercard-url=\"/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/2129/hovercard\" href=\"https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/2129\">#2129</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Comparing with previous attempt,<br>\nthis RFC does not impose any format constraint over the contents of the changelog and instead only requires an external URL.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This RFC also reserves the possibility of using a local file included in crate as changelog while leaving it to future RFCs.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3779",
            "title": "RFC: Crate changelog field",
            "date_modified": "2025-03-04T10:56:19.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-02-25T15:03:12.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "kxxt",
                "url": "https://github.com/kxxt"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18526288?u=a851e2ec349404d3ad63a62786fe9a35009fa8d1&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This proposes adding <code class=\"notranslate\">#[inline(trampoline)]</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">#[inline(rarely)]</code> to hint the compiler additional information about <em>why</em> you're marking the function for inlining, to help it hopefully make better choices without the overly-strong hammers of <code class=\"notranslate\">always</code> or <code class=\"notranslate\">never</code>.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/scottmcm/rfcs/blob/more-inline-options/text/3778-inline-intents.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3778",
            "title": "RFC: Add additional `inline` intents",
            "date_modified": "2025-03-14T17:05:39.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-02-23T01:53:45.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "scottmcm",
                "url": "https://github.com/scottmcm"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/138764211?u=fd6e1047bcae81137b81095986a8ab16ca3d8914&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">Rust should have a spaceship operator <code class=\"notranslate\">&lt;=&gt;</code> for cleaner three-way comparisons.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/bjoernager/rfcs/blob/spaceship-operator/text/3776-spaceship-operator.md\">Rendered</a>.</p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3776",
            "title": "RFC: Add \"spaceship\" operator.",
            "date_modified": "2025-03-01T22:47:53.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-02-21T17:38:16.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "bjoernager",
                "url": "https://github.com/bjoernager"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5963049?u=9241cef72c870a195c728bc4992f8d1fd01968f1&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This RFC guarantees the representation of <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;str</code> and <code class=\"notranslate\">&amp;[T]</code> to be equivalent to a <code class=\"notranslate\">repr(C)</code> struct containing a pointer and a length.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/cramertj/rfcs/blob/slice-repr/text/0000-guaranteed-slice-repr.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
            "url": "https://github.com/rust-lang/rfcs/pull/3775",
            "title": "Guarantee slice representation",
            "date_modified": "2025-03-07T20:30:31.000Z",
            "date_published": "2025-02-19T00:12:13.000Z",
            "author": {
                "name": "cramertj",
                "url": "https://github.com/cramertj"
            }
        },
        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1178779?u=4bd8c56dac06b90d985b2688ec76f0859f297404&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><p dir=\"auto\">This adds an RFC proposing a new attribute that would help detect mistakes when a parameter of a function is not used after the function returns. E.g. when inserting into a collection that is then immediately dropped.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Cc <a class=\"user-mention notranslate\" data-hovercard-type=\"user\" data-hovercard-url=\"/users/joshtriplett/hovercard\" data-octo-click=\"hovercard-link-click\" data-octo-dimensions=\"link_type:self\" href=\"https://github.com/joshtriplett\">@joshtriplett</a></p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><a href=\"https://github.com/Kixunil/rust-rfcs/blob/must-use-output/text/3773-must-use-output.md\">Rendered</a></p>",
